{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"4af037d269359ef8f38c3a25eacf00c16b077815ccb769689018745ab923c354","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar config schema and identity signing infrastructure","key_entities":["src/rebar/_config_schema.py","rebar.toml","reconciler.baseline_dual_write","reconciler.baseline_consumer_swap","progressive_drift_refresh","remediation_mode","novelty_drop_active","verify.require_signature_for_close","compact.emit_legacy_signature_mirror","verify.completion_floor_active","src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_translate.py","_seam.append_event","_apply_authorship","_write_event_file","identity.signing_key","sshsig.sign","/rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key","REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY","REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY"],"problem_keywords":["config pruning","settled rollout flags","feature activation","authenticated identity","signing key provisioning","doc accuracy"],"propositions":["Seven config keys (baseline_dual_write, baseline_consumer_swap, progressive_drift_refresh, remediation_mode, novelty_drop_active, verify.require_signature_for_close, compact.emit_legacy_signature_mirror) must be removed from schema and rebar.toml after rollout settlement.","verify.completion_floor_active must be activated in this project's rebar.toml after validation (30/30 gold-set, κ=1.0).","Ticket-event writers (local dev, AWS review-bot, AWS auto-lander, GitHub Actions reconciler) must each be configured with a signing identity delivery path for author_id/author_email/author_sig stamping.","The reconciler's _write_event_file must inline-stamp and sign author fields before persisting, reusing _apply_authorship logic, without routing through _seam.append_event to preserve batch-commit orchestration.","Private signing keys must be provisioned per environment: local dev via ~/.ssh path in config, AWS via SSM SecureString /rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key materialized to /run/secrets/ at boot, GitHub Actions via encrypted secret written to mktemp with 0600 permissions.","All config documentation, migration guides, and release notes must be swept to remove references to the seven pruned keys and reflect the authenticated-identity design."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785821763701395230,"uuid":"08a9e6eb-3adb-4be5-8dcb-a763e45a7810"}